":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the live-visibility verdict is surfaced when --live-visibility is passed (new JSON field + schema/contract-test update, or a separate advisory stream) so the mechanism's data flow is complete without silently breaking the pinned bridge_fsck.schema.json required-key contract.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC: 'default rebar bridge fsck (no --live-visibility) JSON contract is unchanged (exactly unknown_event_types, binding_drift, store_integrity)'","src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json:8 '\"required\": [\"unknown_event_types\", \"binding_drift\", \"store_integrity\"]'","tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_outputs.py and test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py:121 assert exactly this key set","ABSENCE: plan never says whether --live-visibility adds a JSON field or a side channel"],"finding":"The mechanism under-specifies how the live-visibility verdict is surfaced when --live-visibility IS passed. The plan pins the default (no-flag) JSON as exactly {unknown_event_types, binding_drift, store_integrity} (matching the pinned bridge_fsck.schema.json 'required' set and schema-contract tests), but does not state whether the flag path adds a new JSON field (which would require a schema + contract-test update) or emits the advisory verdict on a separate stream. Without this, the mechanism's data flow for the active-flag case is incomplete.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fac69ee2d228b8917","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope constraint #5 / AC lines 1 & 5","norm_id":"n62105c7723aa9e26","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds a 'live_visibility' key to the JSON output under --live-visibility, tripping the pinned schema/contract tests","Implementer chooses a stderr advisory but a downstream operator expects it in JSON"],"severity":"c